The board of elections of Towns County shall be composed of five members, each of whom shall be an elector and resident of the county and who shall be selected in the following manner:
(1) Two members of the board shall be selected by the chairperson of the county executive committee of the political party which received the highest number of votes within the county for its candidate for President of the United States in the general election immediately preceding the appointment of the member. Each selection shall have been ratified by a majority of the members of the executive committee voting at a regular scheduled meeting or at a meeting duly called and held for such purpose; selected name to be submitted to the governing authority of the county for appointment as members of the election board for Towns County;
(2) Two members of the board shall be selected by the chairperson of the county executive committee of the political party which received the second highest number of votes within the county for its candidate for President of the United States in the general election immediately preceding the appointment of the member. Each selection shall have been ratified by a majority of the members of the executive committee voting at a regularly scheduled meeting or at a meeting duly called and held for such purpose; selected names to be submitted to the governing authority of the county for appointment as members of the election board for Towns County;
(3) The fifth member of the board of elections shall be appointed by the Judge of the Superior Court. Said appointment shall be made from a list of three names to be submitted to by the Grand Jury to the Judge of Superior Court. Said member shall not be an officer or member of the executive committee of any political party at the time of such member's selection or at any time during such member's term of office as a member of the board of elections.

